  "verdict": "The determinism pad buys nothing and costs throughput where it engages. Depth 3 warm: c16 747.6 (16/16), c32 807.5 (32/32), c64 683.7 (62/64) against 750.8 / 827.3 / 789.2 (61/64) with the pad off, i.e. 13% slower at 64 users for no identity gain. No speculation warm: c64 1263.3 (64/64) against 1268.4 (64/64), i.e. inert. The arithmetic explains it: without speculation 64 users is 64 decode rows, below the pad's 128-row threshold, so the pad never engages and the row-invariant kernel is already exact; with depth 3 the verify step submits up to 256 rows, the pad engages and pads them, and the residual flips above 16 users survive. Those flips are therefore not GEMM row-tier effects. The published configuration keeps the pad off."
 },
